note contract 5 fresh, lines 124 and 127 with 4 lines 93-98: an inline callee that writes every
note element at constant indexes (after inlining and unrolling) leaves all bits written, and only
note non-inline calls are error 27. ASSUMPTION (README A3): `to void inline` is valid and the analysis
note sees through the inlined body. stdout s[5] = 7, then 2+..+9 = 44 (exp/f5-inline.out).
om2
fn fill t edit uchar 8 b uchar to void inline
for i ulong 8 unroll
put t i add b uchar i
end
end
fn f s edit uchar 8 fresh k ulong to ulong
fill s 2
acc = ulong 0
for j ulong 8
acc = add acc ulong get s j
end
putd ulong get s k
ret acc
end
fn main to int
a = new uchar 8 0
putd f a 5
ret 0
end
